    },
    {
      "muscleGroup": "Shoulders",
      "severity": "mild",
      "observation": "Shoulders account for only 10.4% of total volume with 4 sets, making them the smallest dedicated muscle group block outside of arms. For balanced upper body development alongside chest and back, gradually increasing shoulder volume over coming periods would be beneficial."
    }
  ],
  "deloadRecommended": false,
  "deloadReason": null,
  "actionItems": [
    "Continue applying progressive overload on your main lifts — aim to add a small amount of weight or one extra rep on at least one set per muscle group next period, building on this week's across-the-board strength index gains.",
